From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux apps keep the screen on

Video players, games, presentations and downloads ask the desktop to keep
the screen on or the device awake: through xdg-desktop-portal's Inhibit
portal (Flatpak apps, GTK 4's gtk_application_inhibit) or
org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver (browsers, SDL, mpv, Steam). Both are
xdg-desktop-portal-nickel's, which asks Chrome:

- VmApplicationsService.NickelInhibit(app id, app name, reason, flags,
  h socket). NickelInhibit takes a ChromeOS wake lock, as Chrome's own
  tabs do (powerd): "idle" keeps the screen on, "suspend" the device
  awake. The lock lasts while the socket stays open; the backend closes it
  when the app lets go, quits or crashes.

